[# docs-src/repos/cx-registry.cxd — the package index's page,
   repo-cx-registry.html (RULED: DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 4). Facts
   from the registries; the repository has no corpus of its own, so the one
   example is the application host's case over the store shape the index
   is laid out in (the xap-dist suite) — the substitution RESULTS.md names. #]

[repo name=cx-registry
  [intro
    """A git repository is a package registry, and the review is
       the publish gate. `cx-registry` is the package index: a `file://` CX
       store laid out in a repository — content trees, sealed manifests and
       `name@version` aliases — the publisher identity that signs them, and
       the publish program that seals, signs, publishes and re-verifies in
       one run. No service is needed to consume it: clone it, open the
       store, install by alias."""]
  [body
    """Integrity is the artifact's, never the transport's: a package is a
       canonical content tree addressed by its hash, a manifest sealed
       beside it — the tag-object pattern — and a publisher's signature over
       that hash; a released alias is immutable, so a new artifact is a new
       version and a rollback is a hash identity rather than a guess.
       Publishing is a reviewed commit: run the program, commit the new
       store objects and the alias, open the pull request. Consuming runs
       the whole verification chain offline on every install, and vendoring
       is a store clone."""]
  [body
    """The same objects re-host without re-packaging: the next stage serves
       the store over the wire, discovery becomes a catalog query pushed down
       to the store, and fetch, verify and install run by hash exactly as
       before. The guide's [[dist-registry]] and [[dist-consuming]] chapters
       walk the two sides; the verbs are the application host's, which is
       where the corpus that grades them lives."""]
  [gives
    """No module and no V code: the repository is a store, a key document
       and one program written over the application host's package verbs
       and the store, so the table below is the generator's note. What it
       gives you is the index itself, and the shape every later stage
       keeps."""]
  [try
    """The store object a package is: two content trees built from the same
       entries named in two orders, put into a store, one hash — canonical
       order is the tree's, not the author's, which is why re-publishing
       identical sources yields byte-identical objects. The case is the
       application host's; the store it writes to is the store the index
       lays out on disk."""]
  [fixture id=xap-dist-001-tree-canonical-order]
  [status
    """The front door pins nothing of the index — it is consumed by `file://`
       and by the wire, not compiled in — so the registry row carries an
       `at=` and `deps.cxd` carries no row, and the figure draws the
       repository alone. Its own pin document names what it builds on; a
       publish is a pull request against it."""]]
